Chapter: PunctualMutualRecursion

 Two punctual functions that recurse through each other: ping calls
 pong, pong calls ping. Neither is self-recursive, so the per-def
 CDX6005 scan passes each in isolation, yet the pair has unbounded
 execution. The call-graph cycle check must reject at least one of
 them with CDX6005. A three-hop cycle (a -> b -> c -> a) is included
 to exercise the transitive reach walk beyond a single hop.

Section: Definitions

  punctual ping : Integer -> Integer
  ping (n) =
   if n == 0 then 0 else pong (n - 1)

  punctual pong : Integer -> Integer
  pong (n) =
   if n == 0 then 1 else ping (n - 1)

  punctual a3 : Integer -> Integer
  a3 (n) = if n == 0 then 0 else b3 (n - 1)

  punctual b3 : Integer -> Integer
  b3 (n) = c3 (n + 1)

  punctual c3 : Integer -> Integer
  c3 (n) = a3 (n - 2)

  opening : Integer = 0
